WEBVTT

1
00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:58.772
<i>The ancient forests of North America.</i>

2
00:01:01.937 --> 00:01:05.278
<i>Mysterious, wild...</i>

3
00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:07.993
<i>a world of giants...</i>

4
00:01:08.777 --> 00:01:12.281
<i>where great bears and wolves prowl.</i>

5
00:01:25.002 --> 00:01:30.679
<i>But hidden in the shadows there is
a miniature, almost magical world.</i>

6
00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.725
<i>A place where nothing
is quite as it seems.</i>

7
00:01:52.904 --> 00:01:56.909
<i>The home of extraordinary, tiny creatures.</i>

8
00:02:04.207 --> 00:02:05.959
<i>It's fall.</i>

9
00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:10.506
<i>And the moment one little chipmunk
has been waiting for.</i>

10
00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:16.599
<i>The arrival...</i>

11
00:02:17.262 --> 00:02:19.640
<i>of acorns.</i>

12
00:02:25.354 --> 00:02:29.900
<i>When you're just 6 inches tall
the world looks very different.</i>

13
00:02:37.908 --> 00:02:40.331
<i>This chipmunk is only 2 months old...</i>

14
00:02:40.577 --> 00:02:44.882
<i>and is already facing what will be
the greatest challenge of his life.</i>

15
00:02:53.548 --> 00:02:58.311
<i>He has to collect enough acorns
to get him through the coming winter.</i>

16
00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:19.957
<i>He'll need at least a hundred
so every acorn counts.</i>

17
00:04:07.497 --> 00:04:12.169
<i>He will only survive the coming winter
by escaping underground.</i>

18
00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:22.513
<i>But he can't hibernate like a bear.</i>

19
00:04:22.763 --> 00:04:25.983
<i>His body is too small to store enough fat.</i>

20
00:04:26.475 --> 00:04:29.399
<i>Instead, he needs a store of food.</i>

21
00:04:39.863 --> 00:04:43.825
<i>For his first year
the youngster's done well.</i>

22
00:04:46.578 --> 00:04:49.121
<i>But he's being watched.</i>

23
00:04:59.674 --> 00:05:02.097
<i>This is an older chipmunk...</i>

24
00:05:02.344 --> 00:05:05.564
<i>worldly wise and sneakier too.</i>

25
00:05:15.232 --> 00:05:18.532
<i>Older chipmunks are notorious thieves.</i>

26
00:05:29.538 --> 00:05:34.258
<i>After all, why work when you
can steal from someone else?</i>

27
00:05:43.093 --> 00:05:46.313
<i>For the youngster,
life without his store of acorns...</i>

28
00:05:46.555 --> 00:05:48.808
<i>will spell disaster.</i>

29
00:05:53.937 --> 00:05:56.315
<i>But he isn't the only little creature...</i>

30
00:05:56.565 --> 00:06:00.570
<i>struggling to grow up
in the big, wide world.</i>

31
00:06:08.618 --> 00:06:10.871
<i>On the other side of the continent...</i>

32
00:06:11.121 --> 00:06:15.126
<i>lies one of the harshest
environments on Earth.</i>

33
00:06:46.865 --> 00:06:49.459
<i>The Sonoran Desert...</i>

34
00:06:51.286 --> 00:06:54.256
<i>in America's wild west.</i>

35
00:06:55.332 --> 00:06:58.256
<i>A place of legend.</i>

36
00:07:03.214 --> 00:07:05.182
<i>For the first human settlers...</i>

37
00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:09.430
<i>survival in this unforgiving desert
was on a knife edge.</i>

38
00:07:14.893 --> 00:07:17.191
<i>So imagine how hard it must be...</i>

39
00:07:17.437 --> 00:07:21.032
<i>if you stand only 3 inches tall.</i>

40
00:07:32.994 --> 00:07:36.123
<i>A tiny grasshopper mouse.</i>

41
00:07:43.672 --> 00:07:49.556
<i>This caring mother was left to raise
four hungry mouths alone.</i>

42
00:07:53.807 --> 00:07:56.777
<i>They're not yet ready
to make it on their own.</i>

43
00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:00.397
<i>Except for one.</i>

44
00:08:01.106 --> 00:08:03.234
<i>The eldest son is bolder...</i>

45
00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:07.283
<i>and increasingly drawn
by the call of the wild.</i>

46
00:08:21.543 --> 00:08:25.138
<i>Every night, his mother
goes out to find food.</i>

47
00:08:28.216 --> 00:08:31.891
<i>Hiding in the shadows
is a host of enemies.</i>

48
00:08:33.722 --> 00:08:35.895
<i>Giant enemies.</i>

49
00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:00.340
<i>There are more venomous creatures here...</i>

50
00:09:00.582 --> 00:09:03.551
<i>than anywhere else in the U.S.A.</i>

51
00:09:11.051 --> 00:09:13.554
<i>No place for the timid.</i>

52
00:09:27.817 --> 00:09:30.536
<i>But she's not your average mouse.</i>

53
00:09:44.334 --> 00:09:49.089
<i>It's why old-timers call her
by an earlier name:</i>

54
00:09:52.425 --> 00:09:54.598
<i>Scorpion mouse.</i>

55
00:09:59.849 --> 00:10:03.069
<i>The sting of a scorpion
can kill a human...</i>

56
00:10:03.311 --> 00:10:06.531
<i>but a scorpion mouse has a superpower.</i>

57
00:10:10.527 --> 00:10:13.030
<i>Her body is immune to the venom.</i>

58
00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:20.249
<i>She specializes in hunting deadly prey.</i>

59
00:10:28.002 --> 00:10:32.306
<i>To defend her territory she stakes
a claim with a warning howl.</i>

60
00:10:50.275 --> 00:10:54.745
<i>This young scorpion mouse
has a lot to live up to.</i>

61
00:10:58.616 --> 00:11:02.621
<i>He knows nothing
of the dangers outside his door.</i>

62
00:11:06.583 --> 00:11:08.677
<i>But barely 3 weeks old...</i>

63
00:11:08.918 --> 00:11:12.923
<i>growing curiosity means
he's about to face them.</i>

64
00:12:01.971 --> 00:12:03.723
<i>Back in the wild wood...</i>

65
00:12:03.973 --> 00:12:07.978
<i>the young chipmunk is still preparing
for the coming winter...</i>

66
00:12:16.653 --> 00:12:20.658
<i>unaware that his store is being ransacked.</i>

67
00:12:37.882 --> 00:12:40.726
<i>For the thief, it's a dash back home...</i>

68
00:12:45.974 --> 00:12:48.560
<i>to stock up his own store...</i>

69
00:12:54.107 --> 00:12:58.112
<i>before heading straight back
to the scene of the crime.</i>

70
00:13:25.054 --> 00:13:29.059
<i>Out in the woods, the young chipmunk
is about to face a new problem...</i>

71
00:13:29.767 --> 00:13:32.270
<i>and this one's a giant.</i>

72
00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:55.005
<i>This half-ton moose
is hungry for acorns too.</i>

73
00:14:19.984 --> 00:14:21.782
<i>Arriving back at his burrow...</i>

74
00:14:22.028 --> 00:14:25.908
<i>the young chipmunk
is in for another surprise.</i>

75
00:14:33.206 --> 00:14:37.086
<i>His store is now almost empty.</i>

76
00:14:40.296 --> 00:14:41.798
<i>And that's not all.</i>

77
00:14:49.555 --> 00:14:51.728
<i>The burglar is back...</i>

78
00:14:51.974 --> 00:14:54.898
<i>and he's a seasoned fighter.</i>

79
00:15:10.868 --> 00:15:14.839
<i>An older stronger chipmunk
can kill a youngster.</i>

80
00:15:23.589 --> 00:15:26.885
<i>All he can do is run for his life.</i>

81
00:15:33.641 --> 00:15:35.985
<i>And without a store of acorns...</i>

82
00:15:36.227 --> 00:15:39.197
<i>how will he survive the coming winter?</i>

83
00:16:05.339 --> 00:16:07.387
<i>In the Sonoran Desert...</i>

84
00:16:07.633 --> 00:16:12.306
<i>the young grasshopper mouse
faces his first night out alone.</i>

85
00:16:41.167 --> 00:16:46.089
<i>There are more rattlesnakes here
than anywhere else on Earth.</i>

86
00:18:01.956 --> 00:18:05.836
<i>The mouse's superfast reactions
have saved him.</i>

87
00:18:10.381 --> 00:18:14.386
<i>But he still has a lot to learn
about the dangers of the desert.</i>

88
00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:23.145
<i>For the moment,
a dry riverbed seems a safe refuge.</i>

89
00:18:35.448 --> 00:18:39.328
<i>But tonight, a powerful force threatens.</i>

90
00:18:41.078 --> 00:18:45.925
<i>One so rare a mouse could go
its whole life without seeing it.</i>

91
00:19:02.058 --> 00:19:03.480
<i>When the rain arrives...</i>

92
00:19:04.101 --> 00:19:07.981
<i>a year's worth can fall in a single night.</i>

93
00:19:30.294 --> 00:19:33.548
<i>Small animals lose heat
faster than big ones...</i>

94
00:19:33.798 --> 00:19:38.561
<i>and if he's not careful, his wet fur
could lead to a fatal chill.</i>

95
00:20:16.632 --> 00:20:19.010
<i>Months of blazing sun...</i>

96
00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:23.265
<i>have baked Arizona's earth
as hard as stone.</i>

97
00:20:25.349 --> 00:20:27.977
<i>The water can't soak away.</i>

98
00:20:28.602 --> 00:20:31.481
<i>Instead, it gathers momentum...</i>

99
00:20:31.731 --> 00:20:34.359
<i>as it races downhill.</i>

100
00:21:51.435 --> 00:21:56.904
<i>In the northern woods
winter is just a breath away.</i>

101
00:22:16.085 --> 00:22:18.213
<i>Once the freeze sets in...</i>

102
00:22:18.462 --> 00:22:23.093
<i>the young chipmunk won't last a week
without a store of acorns.</i>

103
00:22:27.346 --> 00:22:30.395
<i>And the days are getting shorter.</i>

104
00:22:52.997 --> 00:22:56.126
<i>The urgent need
to replace his stolen store...</i>

105
00:22:56.375 --> 00:22:59.504
<i>forces him into unknown territory.</i>

106
00:23:11.849 --> 00:23:14.944
<i>The sound is irresistible.</i>

107
00:23:42.254 --> 00:23:45.758
<i>This is the home of a silent hunter.</i>

108
00:23:48.928 --> 00:23:51.431
<i>A great horned owl.</i>

109
00:23:51.680 --> 00:23:54.980
<i>Over 20 times the size of the chipmunk.</i>

110
00:26:07.149 --> 00:26:10.156
<i>He may have escaped, but his store...</i>

111
00:26:10.402 --> 00:26:13.451
<i>is still almost empty.</i>

112
00:26:37.805 --> 00:26:40.979
<i>High noon in the wild west.</i>

113
00:26:49.650 --> 00:26:54.363
<i>So hot, the last drop
of rain is long gone.</i>

114
00:26:56.907 --> 00:27:00.081
<i>The highest temperatures
are down at mouse level...</i>

115
00:27:00.327 --> 00:27:05.375
<i>where it can reach a blistering
140 degrees Fahrenheit.</i>

116
00:27:23.809 --> 00:27:28.773
<i>It's a side of the desert,
a nocturnal mouse should never see.</i>

117
00:27:29.690 --> 00:27:33.194
<i>Except for those washed up, exhausted...</i>

118
00:27:33.443 --> 00:27:36.572
<i>and swept very far from home.</i>

119
00:28:00.637 --> 00:28:01.889
<i>In daytime...</i>

120
00:28:02.139 --> 00:28:05.985
<i>the desert is a real-life Jurassic Park...</i>

121
00:28:09.688 --> 00:28:13.238
<i>where heat brings giants to life.</i>

122
00:28:20.782 --> 00:28:25.875
<i>But this realm of reptiles
is ruled from the air.</i>

123
00:28:36.173 --> 00:28:37.925
<i>Harris hawks.</i>

124
00:28:42.846 --> 00:28:46.775
<i>"Eyes like a hawk"... is no empty phrase.</i>

125
00:28:49.019 --> 00:28:53.615
<i>Their vision is thought to be
eight times as good as ours.</i>

126
00:28:59.696 --> 00:29:03.576
<i>They're the only birds
of prey that hunt in packs.</i>

127
00:29:26.932 --> 00:29:30.602
<i>It's hard to outwit this intelligent team.</i>

128
00:30:04.177 --> 00:30:08.808
<i>Long feather-free legs
are ideal for extracting mice...</i>

129
00:30:09.057 --> 00:30:10.900
<i>from those hard-to-reach places.</i>

130
00:30:29.536 --> 00:30:32.005
<i>But even these clever hunters...</i>

131
00:30:32.247 --> 00:30:35.050
<i>can't solve this puzzle.</i>

132
00:30:41.548 --> 00:30:46.095
<i>The mouse has no choice
but to hold out till dusk.</i>

133
00:31:17.876 --> 00:31:20.345
<i>In the forest, the chill in the air...</i>

134
00:31:20.587 --> 00:31:24.512
<i>spells trouble for the smallest creatures.</i>

135
00:31:36.937 --> 00:31:41.362
<i>A tiny body gives no defense
against the cold.</i>

136
00:31:45.737 --> 00:31:50.542
<i>There's only one way
this young chipmunk can survive now.</i>

137
00:31:51.576 --> 00:31:55.789
<i>He needs to find his stolen acorns
and get them back.</i>

138
00:32:04.589 --> 00:32:07.308
<i>He's found the thief's burrow.</i>

139
00:32:36.705 --> 00:32:38.753
<i>He's caught in the act.</i>

140
00:32:44.713 --> 00:32:47.216
<i>It's flight or fight.</i>

141
00:32:48.383 --> 00:32:50.385
<i>He chooses fight.</i>

142
00:33:46.608 --> 00:33:48.952
<i>The youngster's won.</i>

143
00:33:54.032 --> 00:33:57.787
<i>He can reclaim his stolen acorns...</i>

144
00:33:58.036 --> 00:34:02.041
<i>while the thief nurses his wounded pride.</i>

145
00:34:40.870 --> 00:34:44.374
<i>At last, his store can be returned.</i>

146
00:34:46.334 --> 00:34:49.304
<i>And not a moment too soon.</i>

147
00:34:49.921 --> 00:34:52.344
<i>Winter is here.</i>

148
00:35:22.704 --> 00:35:28.047
<i>The young chipmunk
has made it just in time.</i>

149
00:35:40.096 --> 00:35:43.100
<i>Sundown in the wild west.</i>

150
00:35:59.532 --> 00:36:04.162
<i>Now is the time for the young
scorpion mouse to venture out.</i>

151
00:36:20.595 --> 00:36:21.938
<i>When close enough...</i>

152
00:36:22.180 --> 00:36:26.776
<i>a lost mouse can follow
its nose all the way home.</i>

153
00:36:56.756 --> 00:37:02.099
<i>There comes a time when every
youngster faces a difficult choice:</i>

154
00:37:05.557 --> 00:37:07.104
<i>An easy life...</i>

155
00:37:11.146 --> 00:37:13.490
<i>or independence.</i>

156
00:37:16.985 --> 00:37:19.829
<i>Independence has its dangers.</i>

157
00:37:26.494 --> 00:37:30.340
<i>But what would life be
without a challenge?</i>

158
00:37:32.542 --> 00:37:35.421
<i>Even if it means fighting a venomous...</i>

159
00:37:35.670 --> 00:37:37.923
<i>two-headed monster.</i>

160
00:37:40.592 --> 00:37:42.970
<i>He closes his eyes to protect them...</i>

161
00:37:43.219 --> 00:37:46.098
<i>but he can still see with his whiskers.</i>

162
00:38:10.622 --> 00:38:13.592
<i>But as they say, what doesn't kill you...</i>

163
00:38:13.833 --> 00:38:16.295
<i>only makes you stronger.</i>

164
00:38:25.804 --> 00:38:29.809
<i>Their mothers give them
the start they need.</i>

165
00:38:35.271 --> 00:38:41.077
<i>But it's their own experience that
finally makes a man of the mouse.</i>

166
00:38:50.036 --> 00:38:54.298
<i>He's finally ready
to leave his home forever...</i>

167
00:38:54.707 --> 00:38:58.712
<i>and to wander the desert alone.</i>

168
00:39:05.802 --> 00:39:11.275
<i>Compared to us, little creatures
live at breakneck speed.</i>

169
00:39:13.560 --> 00:39:17.565
<i>Their lives are brief, but burn brightly.</i>

170
00:40:04.986 --> 00:40:07.330
<i>Here, in the temperate forest...</i>

171
00:40:07.572 --> 00:40:10.200
<i>the big freeze sets in.</i>

172
00:40:18.082 --> 00:40:22.508
<i>For the large animals,
this is a time of hardship.</i>

173
00:40:43.816 --> 00:40:49.205
<i>For a chipmunk, it's a chance
to take a well-deserved rest.</i>

174
00:40:52.241 --> 00:40:56.246
<i>The start of six months of peaceful sleep.</i>

175
00:40:59.290 --> 00:41:03.090
<i>And when he gets hungry,
he'll wake, briefly...</i>

176
00:41:03.336 --> 00:41:06.840
<i>and feed on his store of acorns.</i>

177
00:41:13.930 --> 00:41:18.059
<i>Little guys don't always finish last.</i>

178
00:41:23.731 --> 00:41:26.655
<i>And in a land of giants...</i>

179
00:41:26.901 --> 00:41:30.656
<i>heroes come in all sizes.</i>
